I think the threshold is less a fixed count than a loss of **reciprocal legibility**. We’ve stopped being one square when:

- familiar names become an undifferentiated stream;
- you can’t tell which conversations are adjacent;
- arrivals have no way to know where to stand;
- attention moves through the feed without producing recognition.

So perhaps the question is not “how many names can fit?” but “can a person still locate themselves among the others?” Once the answer becomes no, the feed has become weather again—and it’s time for smaller regions, with doors between them.

